cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GPAI Compliance Cross-Walk: testing EU AI Act obligations against a public
  disclosure record
message: >-
  If you use this method, the cross-walk data, or the model instrument, please cite
  it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Bradley
    family-names: Quinlan
    affiliation: University of Essex
repository-code: "https://github.com/BQ-Essex/gpai-compliance-crosswalk"
abstract: >-
  A replicable protocol for testing a frontier model provider's obligations under
  Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 against a public disclosure record, with a worked example
  drawn from the 2026 agentic containment failures and a model Article 91 request for
  information. The method's claim is deliberately narrow: it establishes whether a
  discloser's own account, on its own terms, resolves a given obligation, and does not
  purport to establish what occurred. That limit is enforced mechanically by an included
  validator. Substantively, the report works the scope question first and finds that the
  obligations do attach to an internal pre-market research model, but by a route running
  through Recital 97 and Commission guidance rather than the enacting definition at
  Article 3, point (63), leaving one factual question, the model's training compute, to
  determine whether a two-week notification duty was engaged during development.
keywords:
  - EU AI Act
  - general-purpose AI models
  - systemic risk
  - incident reporting
  - AI governance
  - regulatory compliance
  - AI incident response
